ID: vr-61
Title: Evidence-led profiling during real use of this chat's head

Status: DONE
Milestone: Post-M1 live-use observation
Dependencies: vr-57

Purpose:
  Measure this chat's explicitly opted-in live Claire/Hazel instance without
  confusing development captures, other apps or total-machine load with its cost.

Tasks:
  Retain exact owned process-tree identity and current visual/voice settings.
  Sample private committed memory, working set and CPU in bounded idle/speech lanes.
  Record actual playback preparation/completion timing and cache outcomes.
  Keep receipts private, separate test contention and create evidence-backed
    finite improvement workstreams without silently lowering requested quality.
  Deliver concise findings through this session's speaking head and written docs.

Acceptance criteria:
  No new head/restart, user-profile automation, recording, transcript persistence,
    scheduler or always-running profiler required for observation.
  Distinguish process-tree CPU from total-machine CPU and private commit from RAM.
  Record measurement interval, source/runtime identity and concurrency limitations.
  Only measured or source-traced opportunities become TODOs; no fabricated gains.

Completion evidence:
  Prior five-second observation: eight owned processes, 887.3 MiB private commit
    and approximately 0.97% machine-normalized CPU. Not a controlled comparison.
  .local\qualification\live-use-01\receipt.json: same eight-process tree, one-second
    samples; idle12.008s/0.065% machine-normalized head CPU/887.04MiB private mean.
    Uncached useful animated summary: start21.412s/total30.220s, completed.
    Generation-labelled22.220s/11.73% CPU; playing-labelled8.034s/2.674% CPU.
    Whole-machine CPU42.17% idle/52.31% generation; other machine work is real
    uncontrolled contention, not attributed to Verona. No development capture
    ran during measurement; shared manager excluded. Not a controlled benchmark.
    New bounded vr62 latency/vr63 complete-tree-memory investigations retain
    exact limitations rather than claiming improvements or a proved leak.
  Concise findings actually spoken through the existing head and completed.
    Follow-up narration during gallery capture is labelled contention, not
    comparable clean evidence. Chapter07 records observations/interpretation.
    vr-62/#61 and vr-63/#62 are independently tracked Open/Todo investigations;
    neither is an implemented latency/memory improvement.

Completion log:
  2026-11-21 - Owner explicitly requests real-session performance observation and
